{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1247578-what-to-read-while-waiting","id":1247578,"title":"What to read while waiting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-18T18:38:21-07:00","id":1247578,"title":"What to read while waiting","content":"Years ago I had a hankering to play Mage and grabbed up any traditionally printed book I could find that wasn't ridiculously overpriced. I ran a couple sessions for my gaming group but they were not terribly into it and a lot of my books never even got opened and we went back to Vampire.<br /> <br /> I have decided I want to give it another go and have ordered the 2nd. edition book, which I have heard will fix some of my group gripes. While it is being assembled and loaded onto a slow boat to Australia, I though I would get some reading done on any 1st ed. books which are still relevant. Anyone have any suggestions from this list?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/wcaOhOa\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/wcaOhOa\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/wcaOhOa\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/gallery/wcaOhOa </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/142-thiassi","name":"Thiassi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T18:59:22-07:00","id":1247582,"title":"","content":"In no particular order:<br /> <br /> Sanctum and Sigil can be good for the Mage politics on a Consilium level.<br /> <br /> The conceptual stuff in Astral Realmd is still very relevant.<br /> <br /> Keys to the Supernal Tarot and Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss are chock full of things you can hook into stories, but they\u2019ll require updating to 2e mechanics if you use them as more than just inspiration.<br /> <br /> Adamantine Arrow can probably be useful for its description of how a Caucus can be set up and you can extrapolate from there and combine with the Order philosophies in the 2e book get an idea of how regional Mage politics are.<br /> <br /> Reign of the Exarch has a decent skeleton to hang a Chronicle on, I have a friend that\u2019s been running it for the last three almost four years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T19:04:09-07:00","id":1247584,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick response. Just one more thing.<br /> Is there anything in the new book which straight up contradicts or supersedes anything in the older books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/142-thiassi","name":"Thiassi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T20:35:28-07:00","id":1247599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiassi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1247578-what-to-read-while-waiting?p=1247584#post1247584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the quick response. Just one more thing.<br /> Is there anything in the new book which straight up contradicts or supersedes anything in the older books?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Besides Mechanically? As far as I can tell, not overly. They have been pretty good with that. They have provided more concrete origins for the orders as opposed to &quot;maybe they came from Atlantis maybe they didn't.&quot; Dark Eras goes into more detail but the diamond formed around the time of Alexander the Great and Seers are a splinter group of the silver ladder. Overall plot elements are always up to the Story teller so it's up to you if any of that matters.<br /> Most changes were made to make the game flow a bit easier. Like Mage armour as an attainment or spells no longer being designated covert or vulgar. That sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T07:23:15-07:00","id":1247692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiassi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1247578-what-to-read-while-waiting?p=1247584#post1247584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the quick response. Just one more thing.<br /> Is there anything in the new book which straight up contradicts or supersedes anything in the older books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, however there's a lot that is recontextualised and modified. For example, Convocations are detailed in the Silver Ladder book. 2e alters some aspects of them and makes them far more important, but you still really need the original Silver Ladder book to really get an idea how they work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T11:45:06-07:00","id":1247765,"title":"","content":"Magical Traditions is now basically a load of tosh.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, not entirely true, but the notion behind the majority of the book is very off base.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oops, not a problem, you actually have a list and that's not in there. My bad, missed that. ^_^;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-19-2018, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T13:47:16-07:00","id":1247798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1247578-what-to-read-while-waiting?p=1247765#post1247765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magical Traditions is now basically a load of tosh.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, not entirely true, but the notion behind the majority of the book is very off base.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oops, not a problem, you actually have a list and that's not in there. My bad, missed that. ^_^;</div> </div> </div> </div>how is that btw? would any of them still work as style merits or is it completely obsolete lorewise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T15:33:44-07:00","id":1247827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1247578-what-to-read-while-waiting?p=1247798#post1247798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> how is that btw? would any of them still work as style merits or is it completely obsolete lorewise?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have largely replaced by dedicated tools, Legacies, and (for those Traditions that joined into the Free Council) Techne. The book's explanations of how the traditions worked was always kind of at odds with the way Awakening's magic work and really has no place with the clarified stance of 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T16:30:18-07:00","id":1247837,"title":"","content":"Glad for the clarification! Thanks!","sig